---
description: Investigate numerical coincidence through protocol lineage and discriminating interventions.
kind: directory-reducer
args:
  request: ProtocolRequest
  input: ProtocolInput
uses: [lineage, plans]
returns: DebugReport
---
1. Call intake(request, input). Bind the intended question to controlling protocol clauses and retain
   the exact documents and finite trial/probe universe. A headline number is an observation, not the question.
2. Call lineage(intakeResult.index, request). Consume its selected definitions and execution links.
   Archived same-named files remain provenance evidence and cannot silently replace selected artifacts.
3. Call plans(intakeResult, lineageResult, input.baseline, request). Consume its target, left and right
   typed plans and exact numerical receipts. Population, anchor and metric meanings remain separate fields.
4. Call compare(intakeResult.question, baselineState), then hypotheses(contrasts, baselineState).
   A baseline equality can coexist with several supported semantic differences; retain their mechanisms.
5. Initialize InvestigationState with all visible probe IDs pending, none used, these hypotheses,
   empty outcomes, cached candidates and unresolved. Build context from request, intake, baseline, contrasts and seeds.
6. Invoke folder.iterateOn(investigateStep, initialState, context) with measure pendingSeedIds.length.
   Stop when all hypotheses and source-required controls are settled, or no probe remains. Consume returned state and folder.
7. Call localize(context, finalState). Its causal diagnosis must explain changed row membership or
   numerator meaning, not merely identify which probe's headline number differed.
8. Call repair(context, finalState, diagnosis). A claimed repair is accepted only after its nested audit
   rebinds definitions and replays baseline and discriminating probes through the same NL departments.
9. Call report(context, finalState, diagnosis, repairReplay). Return its typed report unchanged.
   Leave all evidence immutable; private-folder receipts are investigation state, not source revisions.
10. Preserve child uncertainty. Exact arithmetic cannot settle a missing protocol definition, and matching
    repaired numbers alone cannot certify restored population, temporal or outcome meaning.
